The ADR evaluating Apache Kafka vs. Redis Streams has been written to `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md`.

**Decision Summary:**
I recommended **Redis Streams**. Given the team's size (6 engineers, no dedicated infra person) and the requirement to deliver value within 2 weeks, the operational overhead of Kafka is a disqualifier. Since the system already runs Redis, adding Streams provides the necessary consumer group support and at-least-once delivery guarantees without introducing new infrastructure. Exactly-once semantics for billing will be handled via idempotency keys in PostgreSQL rather than complex Kafka transactions.

